    "title": "Hazardous road conditions for parts of the Coulee Region Thursday morning; Tracking storms in the afternoon and evening",
    "text": "Tonight, our next system brings a mess of multiple precipitation types across the region. While all precipitation types on the table, snow accumulation will be little to none. Freezing rain will be the main hazard. Up to 0.4\" of ice can accumulate, mainly towards Jackson County. This will make for slippery to near impossible travel conditions across the region. With risks to travel, winter weather alerts are in place from midnight Wednesday night through 10 am Thursday morning. An Ice Storm Warning is in effect for Jackson County. Roads will be impossible to travel at times with significant ice accumulation, as well as minor accumulations of snow and sleet.A Winter Weather Advisory is in effect for La Crosse, Monroe, Winona, Buffalo, Trempealeau, Fillmore, Houston, Vernon, and Richland County. Roads may be slippery at times due to ice accumulating, as well as a bit of accumulation of snow and sleet. Rain will begin to transition to a wintry mix overnight. This wintry mix will be mainly for areas near and north of I-90, with snow, sleet, and freezing rain at times. As we head into the late morning and afternoon, the wintry mix transitions back to rain showers. Rain will be occasional at times, with some storms possibly becoming strong to severe. Stronger storms are more likely in areas southeast of La Crosse. Damaging winds and a few spin-ups are the main risks with small hail and downpours as secondary hazards. All in all the wintry mix to storms on Thursday will amount to 0.5\" to 2\"+ of precipitation.",
